## Root cause
$ finch vm stop; finch vm status
Stopped
$ time finch version
Client: Version v1.19.0 ... Server: containerd v2.2.1, runc 1.4.0
real 11.836s, exit 0
$ finch vm status
Running
# finch v1.19.0 starts a stopped VM on `finch version` (and on `finch info`) and exits 0 once it is up
# (~11.8 s here). The design's premise ("`finch version` exits non-zero with the VM stopped", from
# finch's source) does not hold on this finch. warden's 10 s bound kills the query mid-start and
# reports "`finch version` failed"; the VM finishes starting anyway, so the next build or doctor
# passes. No slow hint seen: the VM answers after the 10 s bound, not within 3-10 s.

